Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_ncm: restart the TX timer if the TX freelist is empty

Backport Cosmin Tanislav's 2026-08-17 fix:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2608.2/02481.html
Message-ID: 20260817192638.437798-1-cosmin-gabriel.tanislav.xa@renesas.com
Fixes: 6d3865f9d41f ("usb: gadget: NCM: Add transmit multi-frame.")
Driver license and existing copyright: GPL-2.0-or-later.

The networking core retries normal packets on NETDEV_TX_BUSY, but the NCM
timer calls ndo_start_xmit directly. Ignoring BUSY strands a partial NTB
until later traffic fills it. Retry at the existing 300us interval; do not
change successful flushes, teardown, queue sizing or SSH/watchdog policy.

The local callback regression reproduces the lost flush. ROG5 live capture
shows SYN-ACKs delayed under bulk traffic; the deployed callback's assembly
ignores the transmit result. Full physical causality and corrected-kernel
qualification still require a fresh reviewed release. No live hot replacement.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1148,6 +1148,7 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart ncm_tx_timeout(struct hrtimer *data)
 {
 	struct f_ncm *ncm = container_of(data, struct f_ncm, task_timer);
 	struct net_device *netdev = READ_ONCE(ncm->netdev);
+	netdev_tx_t ret;
 
 	if (netdev) {
 		/* XXX This allowance of a NULL skb argument to ndo_start_xmit
@@ -1158,7 +1159,11 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart ncm_tx_timeout(struct hrtimer *data)
 		 *
 		 * This will call directly into u_ether's eth_start_xmit()
 		 */
-		netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		ret = netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		if (ret == NETDEV_TX_BUSY) {
+			hrtimer_forward_now(data, TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS);
+			return HRTIMER_RESTART;
+		}
 	}
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
